{"id":173317628180384,"type":"album","name":"Clouds","artist":"Joni Mitchell","year":1969,"weight":20,"info":{"cover":"https://dn711300.ca.archive.org/0/items/mbid-d5685777-7ef1-4a44-a05e-c316cb8fb002/mbid-d5685777-7ef1-4a44-a05e-c316cb8fb002-7428087736.jpg","kind":"Album","tracks":10,"country":"XE","scaruffi":7.0,"aoty":78,"aoty_user":80,"yt":"J48BpiPLHtA","links":{"spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/album/03iFLgmgkLT7X5gnXVPID5","youtube":"https://music.youtube.com/playlist?list=OLAK5uy_nPYhU3kbWro4oR6kx5o4uuDRTxXt8zFGE","rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/joni-mitchell/clouds","aoty":"https://www.albumoftheyear.org/album/6085-joni-mitchell-clouds.php"},"desc":"Clouds is a stark stunner, a great leap forward for Joni Mitchell. Vocals here are more forthright and assured than on her debut and exhibit a remarkable level of subtle expressiveness. Guitar alone is used in accompaniment, and the variety of playing approaches and sounds gotten here is most impressive. \"The Fiddle and the Drum,\" a protest song that imaginatively compares the Vietnam-era warmongering U.S. government to a bitter friend, dispenses with instrumental accompaniment altogether. The sketches presented of lovers by turns depressive (\"Tin Angel\"), roguish (\"That Song About the Midway\"), and faithless (\"The Gallery\") are vividly memorable. Forthright lyrics ."},"artist_ref":{"id":54285795993713,"name":"Joni Mitchell","info":{"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Joni_Mitchell_2021_Kennedy_Center_Honors_%28cropped%29.jpg?width=500"}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":194427380844280,"type":"genre","name":"Folk Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":621,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":156823753286980,"type":"genre","name":"folk","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":510,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":190318565344926,"type":"genre","name":"Folk Pop","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":248,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":223327500886715,"type":"genre","na